  "style": "Address the user formally (شما, plural verb forms); command labels use the infinitive or verbal noun (باز کردن، ذخیره، بستن). Persian has no capitalisation; use the zero-width non-joiner (U+200C) in compounds such as جست‌وجو and the Persian letters ی and ک, never Arabic ي and ك. Use the Persian comma ، semicolon ؛ and question mark ؟, and the single ellipsis character … after a label that opens a dialog. Latin do-not-translate tokens, numbers, coordinates and key names (Ctrl, Shift, Alt) stay unchanged and left-to-right; isolate them (FSI/PDI or <bdi>) inside Persian text, and keep digits as the format functions produce them. Write menu paths in reading order with \" ◂ \" (for example پرونده ◂ باز کردن) because ▸ is not mirrored in right-to-left text."
